TEST 13587 -- QoS on switchport interface - class set dscp
===========================================================================
Run: 2026-09-22 09:46:04  tb470   policy applied ingress on port2.0.2
Frames are sent with tos=0 and the DSCP is DECODED at egress, so any change
is the DUT marking them, not the sender.

--- enable QoS globally (prompts: 'Traffic will stop ... Continue? (y/n)') ---
configure terminal
Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
IE520-stk(config)#mls qos enable
Traffic will stop while configuration is applied. Continue? (y/n): y
% QoS is already enabled
IE520-stk(config)#  % QoS is already enabled
show mls qos
  Enable
IE520-stk#  show mls qos: Enable | IE520-stk#

--- baseline, no policy ---
  matching src       got=8  dscp=[0]
  non-matching src   got=8  dscp=[0]

--- build class-map / policy-map, set dscp 46 on the matching class ---
configure terminal
Enter configuration commands, one per line.  End with CNTL/Z.
IE520-stk(config)#access-list hardware qacl
IE520-stk(config-ip-hw-acl)#permit ip 10.40.1.1/32 any
IE520-stk(config-ip-hw-acl)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#class-map qcm
IE520-stk(config-cmap)#match access-group qacl
IE520-stk(config-cmap)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#policy-map qpm
IE520-stk(config-pmap)#class qcm
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#set dscp 46
IE520-stk(config-pmap-c)#exit
IE520-stk(config-pmap)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#interface port2.0.2
IE520-stk(config-if)#service-policy input qpm
IE520-stk(config-if)#exit
IE520-stk(config)#end
IE520-stk#  errors: none
show policy-map qpm

  POLICY-MAP-NAME: qpm
    Interfaces: port2.0.2
    Default class-map action: permit

    CLASS-MAP-NAME: default

    CLASS-MAP-NAME: qcm
      QOS-ACCESS-LIST-NAME: qacl
      Set DSCP: 46
